  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The tutorial says any MKR family board; I used the MKR WiFi 1010 (arduino-mkr1000-wifi) mounted on the shield's female headers.",
   "The relays are wired inside the shield to MKR pins 1 and 2. The catalogue's shield card has no pin-1/pin-2 ports, so I made no edge for that. The mkr1-to-shield1 'joined' edge with no ports stands for the whole header stack. I added port-specific edges only for GND, VCC and A1-A4, which the shield card lists.",
   "The circuit image was not available, so the LED wiring is my assumption. Pin 3 goes through a jumper wire to LED_1's anode. Its cathode goes through a 220 ohm resistor to the breadboard ground rail. Pin 4 does the same for LED_2. One jumper wire takes MKR GND to the ground rail. Each series resistor is on the cathode side.",
   "Resistor value (220 ohm) and LED colours are assumed, as the tutorial doesn't give them. At the MKR's 3.3 V logic, 220 ohm keeps each LED pin under the 7 mA limit.",
   "The 24V supply and 24V lamp on the high-power terminals are only an illustrative example in the tutorial, so I did not build them."
